<title>GREECE: GREEK IONIAN BANK PRETAX/PROV. PROFIT DOWN 69PCT.</title>
<headline>GREEK IONIAN BANK PRETAX/PROV. PROFIT DOWN 69PCT.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's state Ionian Bank posted profits before tax and provisions of about 5 billion drachmas in 1996 from 16.5 billion in 1995, down by 69 pct, and it will not pay dividend for fiscal '96, its chairman Haris Stamatopoulos said.</p>
<p>The bank will distribute bonus shares at a ratio to be determined later, he told a news conference.</p>
</text>
